<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Iskander Mirza</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1899">1899</a>–<a href="/years/1969">1969</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Iskander Mirza was a Pakistani soldier and civil servant who became Governor-General in 1955 and the first President of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pakistan">Pakistan</a> in 1956. In October 1958 he abrogated the constitution and declared martial law with army commander <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayub-khan">Ayub Khan</a>, who deposed him within weeks. He died in exile in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/london">London</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/iskander-mirza.jpg" alt="Iskander Mirza" width="260" height="351" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Iskander_Mirza.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
